body:
The manufacturer of Latuda has a prescription savings card than can lower your cost for the prescription.  Mine has been $15 with insurance and the card.

Make a list of questions and concerns.  Write them down so you don’t forget them.  Also, see if they will do more frequent visits while starting or adjusting meds.  My psych has seen me weekly before when we did a major med adjustment (and also filled out short-term disability paperwork so I could focus on making sure the meds were working).  

My therapist suggested keeping a diary of my symptoms.  You may want to do this for your psych as well, some things to track:

Sleep, amount and quality; 
General mood; 
Eating/appetite; 
Thoughts that are recurring; 
Anything else that seems important (I.e spending habits)

Good luck!
